- ## Runtime Requirement
- - `python3` must exist on the host before this skill can run.
- - `node` must exist on the host. QR PNG generation uses local JavaScript execution.
- - Python module `Pillow` must be installed (`python3 -m pip install Pillow`).
- - On macOS/OpenClaw Skills UI, the skill can offer a Homebrew install action for Python 3.
- - On Linux servers, preinstall `python3` and `node` with the system package manager before using this skill.
- 2. Before first use on a server, run `scripts/publisher_cli.py doctor --check-network --strict` and resolve failed checks.
- 3. If there is no valid local session, run `scripts/publisher_cli.py prepare-login` first.
- 4. Prefer the inline QR image fields returned by `prepare-login`: send `chat_image.base64` or `qr_png_data_url` directly in chat, then tell the user exactly: `请使用 Z视介 APP 扫描此二维码登录。`
- 5. After the QR image has been shown in chat, run `scripts/publisher_cli.py wait-login` with the returned `qr_state_file` and wait for scan completion.
- 6. Only fall back to attaching `qr_png_file` when the runtime supports local image attachments but inline base64 delivery is unavailable.
- 7. Do not send only a local file path string to Feishu/Lark chat. The QR image must be sent as actual image content.
- 8. Do not surface the internal QR login API details unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- 9. Build the exact request body as a JSON file matching the operation docs. Pass it with `--input-json`.
- 10. Run one of `publish-article`, `edit-article`, `publish-video`, or `edit-video`.
- 11. If the publish host differs from the bundled default, override it with `--base-url`.
- 12. Run `scripts/release_to_clawhub.py` before sharing the skill on ClawHub. Use `--execute` only when `clawhub` is installed and already authenticated.
