### references/zshijie-api.md  [docs]
- ## Definition Completeness
- - The bundled `zshijie-api.json` now keeps both `path` and non-empty `path_template` for all request definitions used by this skill.
- - The four publish/edit operations also define non-empty `payload_fields` to make the API contract explicit.
- - A top-level `file_upload_interfaces` block is included so upload APIs are part of the contract instead of being omitted.
- - The four HTML docs did not provide dedicated upload endpoint URLs. Upload interface `path_template` values are currently TODO placeholders and must be replaced with your real backend endpoints before enabling them.
- - Signing note:
-   - The QR poll request uses a fixed client-side signing seed extracted from the official login page flow.
-   - This skill keeps that seed in code as an implementation constant, not as a user credential or environment secret.
-   - The `prepare-login` console JSON also includes inline PNG transport fields: `chat_image.base64`, `qr_png_base64`, and `qr_png_data_url`
-   - For Feishu/Lark delivery, prefer those inline fields over sending only a local file path string
- - Historical note: the exported HTML once showed a non-TLS absolute URL for this endpoint.
- - Skill default host: `https://zugcpublish.cztv.com`
- The bundled config defaults the publish and edit host to `https://zugcpublish.cztv.com`.
- ## Upload Note
- - Contract location: `file_upload_interfaces` in `zshijie-api.json`
- - Current status: `pending_real_endpoints`
- - Why pending:
-   - The published article/video/edit endpoints only consume media URLs.
-   - The provided HTML docs do not expose separate image/video upload APIs or multipart request examples.
- - Next action:
-   - Provide the real image/video upload API definitions (method, host, path, headers, body fields, success response sample).
-   - Replace the placeholder upload `path_template` values and set `enabled=true`.
+ - URL in HTML: `http://zugcpublish.cztv.com/dasugc/v1/api/v1/article/editShortArticle`
+ The bundled config defaults the publish and edit host to `http://zugcpublish.cztv.com`.

